  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_27ae57f3",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts three emaciated survivors of Auschwitz, with overlaid text claiming they are '3 jewish prisoners after being liberated by the ussr' and 'auschwitz 1945 colorized'. The intent is to present a historically traumatic event — the liberation of Holocaust survivors — as a subject for aesthetic alteration (colorization) and to frame it with a misleading or trivializing context. The use of the term 'jewish prisoners' in conjunction with the image of suffering individuals, combined with the colorization label, may be intended to normalize or trivialize the horror of the Holocaust by reducing it to a visual novelty. This approach can be seen as hateful because it potentially minimizes the gravity of genocide and victimization by treating the suffering of Jewish people as a subject for aesthetic manipulation rather than historical remembrance. The meme may also implicitly reinforce antisemitic tropes by reducing the victims to a 'colorized' image, which can be interpreted as a form of dehumanization or commodification of trauma. The overall intent is to provoke emotional reaction through juxtaposition — the stark reality of Holocaust survivors is contrasted with the superficial act of colorization, which may be used to mock or trivialize the suffering of Jewish victims.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_488ce1cb"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
